                   r      Reverse sort order
                   v      Toggle preview
                   q      Exit mode

             After a buffer is chosen, ‘%%’ is replaced by the buffer name in
             _t_e_m_p_l_a_t_e and the result executed as a command.  If _t_e_m_p_l_a_t_e is
             not given, "paste-buffer -p -b '%%'" is used.

             --OO specifies the initial sort field: one of ‘time’ (creation),
             ‘name’ or ‘size’.  --rr reverses the sort order.  --ff specifies an
             initial filter: the filter is a format - if it evaluates to zero,
